The VarBlock class is internal and cannot be directly instantiated in the test project due to its protection level. There is no immediate public API or factory visible here to create VarBlock instances for testing.

Given this, I will write a test class inside the same namespace as VarBlock and mark it as internal to access the internal class. This requires the test project to be in the same assembly or have InternalsVisibleTo attribute set for the test assembly. Since I cannot modify the production code, I will write the test class in the same namespace and mark it internal, hoping the test project has access.

I will write tests that verify the Logger.LogError call in the VarBlock constructor when the content length is less than 2, using a mock ILoggerFactory and ILogger.

